{"abstract":[{"text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Checking from a test","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"],"anchor":"Checking-from-a-test"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracking plan is how the people and services that read an app’s events learn what each event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds, so it is only useful while it matches the events. With this test, a change to an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t pass the app’s tests until the plan is exported again, and reviewers see the change as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON diff of the plan. The test’s report also says which changes would break payloads from released"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app versions or records already stored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" checks a ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" against the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"committed in a directory, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan.check(againstDirectory:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does. When they differ, it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records a Swift Testing issue whose comment is the check’s report, the same text the ","type":"text"},{"code":"check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"command prints, and it returns the check either way. A plan that is only out of date fails the test","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a breaking one does: in both cases the committed plan isn’t what exporting the events writes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to an app’s test target, so the check runs wherever the app’s tests do. It imports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift Testing, so it belongs in test targets only. To run the check from the command line or CI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without a test, use the app’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanCommand"},{"text":" executable from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Foundation","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Test func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() throws {","    let directory = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","        .deletingLastPathComponent()","        .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","    expectTrackingPlan(try AppTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: directory)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers exporting the plan this test checks.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlanTesting"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"TrackingPlanTesting","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"m